{"id":"granicus-2-248","platform":"granicus","body":"City Council","name":"City Council","date":"2007-09-11","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://lapuente.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=2&clip_id=248","minutes_url":"https://lapuente.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?view_id=2&clip_id=248","packet_url":"","clip_id":248,"view_id":2,"video_url":"https://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=2&clip_id=248","transcript_url":"","mp4_url":"","mp3_url":"","agenda_text":"City Council\nAGENDA\nla puente City Council\nCOUNCIL CHAMBERS\n15900 EAST MAIN STREET, LA PUENTE\nSeptember 11, 2007\n07:00 PM\nCALL TO ORDER\nROLL CALL\nCOUNCILMEMBERS: Solis, Lujan, Chavez, Storing, Perez\nPLEDGE OF ALLEGIANCE\nRECESS SPECIAL CITY COUNCIL MEETING AND SPECIAL COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT COMMISSION MEETING\nPRESENTATIONS\nMOMENT OF SILENCE IN REMEMBRANCE OF ALL THE PEOPLE WHO LOST THEIR LIVES ON SEPTEMBER 11, 2001\nMOMENT OF SILENCE IN REMEMBRANCE OF ALL THE PEOPLE WHO LOST THEIR LIVES ON SEPTEMBER 11, 2001\nINTRODUCTION OF NEW STAFF MEMBERS\nPRESENTATION OF PROCLAMATION PROCLAIMING SEPTEMBER 23, 2007 THROUGH SEPTEMBER 29, 2007, AS CHILDHOOD INJURY PREVENTION WEEK\nORAL COMMUNICATIONS\nIf you wish to address the City Council or Community Development Commission on an item other than a public hearing matter, please complete the Request for Oral Presentation form and submit it to the City Clerk no later than prior to the conclusion of the first speaker’s remarks. (Ordinance No. 06-843).\nMINUTES OF PREVIOUS CITY COUNCIL MEETINGS\nNone.\nPUBLIC HEARINGS BEFORE THE CITY COUNCIL\nB-1\nCONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING TO ADOPT A RESOLUTION APPROVING AN AGREEMENT WITH CHEVRON ENERGY SOLUTIONS FOR THE DESIGN/RENOVATION OF THE LA PUENTE COMMUNITY CENTER AND THE DESIGN/CONSTRUCTION OF THE LA PUENTE YOUTH LEARNING ACTIVITY CENTER AND APPROVAL OF FINANCING\nIt is recommended that the City Council: (1) open the public hearing; (2) take oral testimony and close the public hearing; (3) adopt the resolution authorizing the Mayor to enter into an Energy Services Contract with Chevron Energy Solutions to perform Design/Renovation of the La Puente Community Center and the Design/Construction of the La Puente Youth Learning Activity Center; and (4) approve financing for the construction thereof.\nUNFINISHED BUSINESS OF THE CITY COUNCIL\nC-1\nCONSIDERATION OF AMENDING RESOLUTION 07-4643 AND APPOINTMENT OF PARKS AND RECREATION COMMISSIONERS\nIt is recommended that the City Council amend Resolution 07-4643 to reflect the City Council’s decision regarding the total amount of Commissioners and/or alternates; and appoint a fifth Commissioner with the remaining three (3) applicants as alternates.\nCITY COUNCIL CONSENT CALENDAR\nAll matters listed under Consent Calendar are considered to be routine in nature and may be enacted by one motion approving the recommendation listed on the Agenda. One or more items may be removed from the Consent Calendar so that said item(s) may be discussed and considered individually by the City Council, if a motion to remove the item(s) is approved by an affirmative vote of a majority of the members of the City Council. Those specific item(s) will be considered as the first item under New Business.\nD-1\nAPPROVAL OF RESOLUTION APPROVING WARRANT REGISTER NO. 1210 FOR FISCAL YEAR 2007-08\nIt is recommended that the City Council adopt the resolution.\nD-2\nAPPROVAL OF NEW PARTICIPANT(S) FOR CDBG HOUSING REHABILITATION (D97301-08) - FISCAL YEAR 2007-08\nThe Screening Commission recommends that the City Council approve the allocations and authorize the Assistant City Manager to execute the necessary documents to implement the Housing Rehabilitation Program in the amount of $17,000.\nD-3\nSECOND READING - EXTENSION OF ORDINANCE NO. 06-856 EXTENDING THE TERMS AND PROVISIONS OF URGENCY ORDINANCE NO. O6-853 - PROHIBITING ESTABLISHMENT OR OPERATION OF \"SMOKE SHOPS\" IN THE CITY OF LA PUENTE (Introduced and title read at meeting of August 28, 2007)\nIt is recommended that the City Council adopt the ordinance extending Ordinance No. 06-856 for an additional year.\nD-4\nAUTHORIZATION TO SOLICIT BIDS FOR PURCHASE OF A NEW 2007 CHEVROLET SILVERADO 2500 HD CLASSIC 2WD FOR THE MAINTENANCE SUPERVISOR\nIt is recommended that the City Council authorize Staff to solicit bids for the purchase of a new 2007 Chevrolet Silverado 2500 HD Classic 2WD Regular Cab 133\" Work Truck and designate Tuesday, October 16, 2007 at 10:00 a.m. as the deadline for receiving bids.\nD-6\nBID AWARD: LOCAL STREET RESURFACING (AMAR, PUENTE, TONOPAH) PROJECT\nIt is recommended that the City Council award the contract for the construction portion of the Local Street Resurfacing (Amar, Puente, Tonopah) Project to Silvia Construction.\nD-7\nCONSIDERATION OF AMENDING THE 2007-2008 BUDGET TO INCLUDE THE COSTS FOR CAPITAL IMPROVEMENT PROGRAM (CIP) TO BE FUNDED UNDER THE SEWER ENTERPRISE FUND AND TO AMEND FUNDING SOURCES OF ALL STREET IMPROVEMENTS CIP PROJECTS\nIt is recommended that the City Council adopt the resolution approving the City's updated Capital Improvement Projects and amend the budget to include the costs for the projects in the City's 2007/2008 Fiscal Year Budget.\nD-8\nAUTHORIZATION TO SOLICIT BIDS FOR TEMPLE AVENUE STREET IMPROVEMENT PROJECT FROM GLENDORA AVENUE TO STIMSON AVENUE\nIt is recommended that the City Council: (1) approve the specifications; and (2) authorize Staff to solicit bids for the Temple Avenue Street Improvement Project from Glendora Avenue to Stimson Avenue.\nD-9\nAWARD OF CONTRACT FOR THE INSTALLATION OF AN AUDIO/VISUAL SYSTEM FOR THE SENIOR CENTER IMPROVEMENTS PROJECT\nIt is recommended that the City Council award the bid to Western Audio Visual Corporation in the amount of $23,809.40 and authorize the Mayor to execute the Agreement with Western Audio Visual Corporation for installation of the Audio/Visual system at the Senior Center.\nITEM PULLED FROM CONSENT CALENDAR FOR SEPARATE CONSIDERATION\nD-5\nAUTHORIZATION TO SOLICIT BIDS FOR PURCHASE OF A NEW 2007 FORD ESCAPE HYBRID FWD FOR THE PUBLIC WORKS DIRECTOR\nNEW BUSINESS TO BE CONSIDERED BY THE CITY COUNCIL\nE-1\nCONSIDERATION OF INTRODUCTION OF AN ORDINANCE INCREASING COUNCIL MEMBERS’ SALARIES PURSUANT TO GOVERNMENT CODE SECTION 36516\nIt is recommended that the City Council: (1) read the ordinance by title only and waive further reading; and (2) introduce the ordinance for subsequent adoption.\nE-2\nCONSIDERATION OF FORMATION OF LA PUENTE PUBLIC FINANCING AUTHORITY\nIt is recommended that the City Council adopt the Resolution authorizing Execution and Delivery of a Joint Exercise of Powers Agreement with the La Puente Community Development Commission, Establishing the La Puente Public Financing Authority.\nE-3\nREQUEST TO CONSTRUCT A MONUMENT IN HONOR OF ALL LOCAL VETERANS FROM EVERY BRANCH OF THE SERVICE ON THE TRIANGLE PROPERTY LOCATED AT THE ENTRANCE OF CENTRAL AVENUE AND ABBEY STREET (Requested by Council Member Solis)\nNone.\nRECESS CITY COUNCIL AND CONVENE THE COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT COMMISSION\nCOUNCIL AB1234 REPORTS\nORAL COMMENTS FROM COUNCIL\nORAL COMMENTS FROM STAFF\nRECONVENE SPECIAL CITY COUNCIL MEETING\nRECESS TO CLOSED SESSION\nF-3\nTHE CITY COUNCIL WILL RECESS TO CLOSED SESSION PURSUANT TO GOVERNMENT CODE SECTION 54957.6\nAGENCY NEGOTIATOR: CAROL COWLEY, CITY MANAGER\nEMPLOYEE ORGANIZATION: SEIU LOCAL 721\nRECONVENE TO OPEN SESSION\nADJOURNMENT\nCopies of reports relating to items on the Agenda are available for public inspection or purchase at City Hall. Questions regarding agenda items may be addressed to the City Clerk at 626/855-1500, extension 503. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you need special assistance to participate in a City meeting or other services offered by the City, please contact the City Clerk's Office. Notification at least 48 hours prior to the meeting or time when services are needed will assist City staff in assuring that reasonable arrangements can be made to provide accessibility to the meeting or service.\n* Meetings of the City Council shall be adjourned no later than 10:30 p.m., unless a motion to supersede the 10:30 time limit to consider some or all of the remaining items listed on the Agenda, or to consider items which have been added to the Agenda in accordance with the provisions of the Ralph M. Brown Act, Government Code Section 54950, et seq., is approved by a majority of the members of the City Council. (Ordinance No. 95-727, effective September 7, 1995.)\ns:\\Cclerk\\Agenda\\Agnda2007\\Agn09-11\\a09 11 07reg\nLA PUENTE CITY COUNCIL SEPTEMBER 11, 2007\nAGENDA PAGE 7","minutes_text":"��\u0011ࡱ\u001a�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000>\u0000\u0003\u0000�� \u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0001\u0000\u0000\u0000����\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0000\u0000\u0000����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\u0000q` \u0004\u0000\u0000�\u0012�\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0010\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000�K\u0000\u0000\u000e\u0000bjbjqPqP\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 \u0004\u0016\u0000;�\u0000\u0000\u0013:\u0001\u0000\u0013:\u0001\u0000\u0014C\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000v\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0