\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000MINUTES \rLA PUENTE CITY COUNCIL� \rREGULAR MEETING OF \rSeptember 11, 2007\r\r\r\rA Regular Meeting of the City Council of the City of La Puente was held in the Council Chambers of City Hall, 15900 East Main Street, La Puente, California, on September 11, 2007, at 7:00 p.m. \r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39545\" \u0014CALL TO ORDER\u0015 \u0007\u0007\rMayor Perez called the�City Council meeting�to�order at 7:00 p.m.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39548\" \u0014ROLL CALL \u0015\u0007\u0007\rCouncil�Members present: Lujan, Chavez, Storing, Perez \rCouncil�Members absent: Solis (arrived at 7:11�p.m.)\r\rStaff Members Present: City Manager Cowley, Assistant City Manager Yamachika, City Attorney Casso, Acting City Clerk Giron, Public Works Director Salas, Finance Director Kim, City Planner Arreola, Acting Recreation Services Director Bistarkey \r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39551\" \u0014PLEDGE OF ALLEGIANCE \u0015\u0007\u0007\rThe pledge of allegiance was led by Council Member Chavez.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=46673\" \u0014RECESS SPECIAL CITY COUNCIL MEETING AND SPECIAL COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT COMMISSION MEETING \u0015\u0007\u0007\rMayor Perez recessed the Special City Council Meeting�at 7:01 p.m.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39554\" \u0014PRESENTATIONS \u0015\u0007\u0007\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39557\" \u0014MOMENT OF SILENCE IN REMEMBRANCE OF ALL THE PEOPLE WHO LOST THEIR LIVES ON SEPTEMBER 11, 2001 \u0015\u0007\u0007\rThe City Council observed a moment of silence in honor of those who lost their lives on September 11, 2001. \r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=46679\" \u0014INTRODUCTION OF NEW STAFF MEMBERS \u0015\u0007\u0007\rCity Manager Cowley introduced two (2) new La Puente staff members, Norma Ramirez, Administrative Secretary, and Maria Galvan, Rehabilitation Grants Specialist.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39560\" \u0014PRESENTATION OF PROCLAMATION PROCLAIMING SEPTEMBER 23, 2007 THROUGH SEPTEMBER 29, 2007, AS CHILDHOOD INJURY PREVENTION WEEK \u0015\u0007\u0007\rCity Manager Cowley affirmed that the Proclamation had been delivered. \r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39563\" \u0014ORAL COMMUNICATIONS \u0015\u0007\u0007\rLeonard Wayne Rose Jr. appeared to speak regarding a thank you note he received from regional elected officials and his upcoming academic plans.\r\rKen Medeiros appeared to speak regarding compensation for elected officials in La Puente. \r\rHenry Nodal thanked�the City for their small gift and noted his�concerns regarding a Code�Enforcement issue.\r\rPat Nodal inquired if the City Attorney�could�assist with Mr.�Nodal�s situation and noted her concern regarding the City Council�s compensation.\r\rCity Attorney Casso noted that he could meet with Mr. Nodal at the Council�s direction.\r\rIn response to an inquiry from Mayor Perez, City Manager Cowley provided background information related to AB 701 (Compensation of City Council).\r\rMayor Perez noted various officials in attendance at tonight�s meeting.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39574\" \u0014MINUTES OF PREVIOUS CITY COUNCIL MEETINGS \u0015\u0007\u0007\rNone.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39577\" \u0014PUBLIC HEARINGS BEFORE THE CITY COUNCIL \u0015\u0007\u0007\rB-1\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39578\" \u0014CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING TO ADOPT A RESOLUTION APPROVING AN AGREEMENT WITH CHEVRON ENERGY SOLUTIONS FOR THE DESIGN/RENOVATION OF THE LA PUENTE COMMUNITY CENTER AND THE DESIGN/CONSTRUCTION OF THE LA PUENTE YOUTH LEARNING ACTIVITY CENTER AND APPROVAL OF FINANCING\u0015 \u0007\u0007\rCity Manager Cowley requested that the City Council open the public hearing, take public testimony, and continue the hearing to September 25, 2007.� Staff was waiting for additional information related to the project�s financing.\r\rMayor Perez opened the public hearing at 7:25 p.m. and continued the public hearing to September 25, 2007.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39583\" \u0014UNFINISHED BUSINESS OF THE CITY COUNCIL \u0015\u0007\u0007\rC-1\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39584\" \u0014CONSIDERATION OF AMENDING RESOLUTION 07-4643 AND APPOINTMENT OF PARKS AND RECREATION COMMISSIONERS \u0015\u0007\u0007\rActing Recreation Services Director Bistarkey gave historical background related to Council�s actions on this item.� City Manager Cowley reviewed Council�s options to amend the resolution�which includes appointing one (1) Commissioner with three (3) alternates, or to reconstitute the Commission to consist of�seven (7) total members.\r\rCity Attorney Casso noted that the Council must first decide how to constitute the Commission, with either five (5) or seven (7) members, prior to appointing any additional members.\r\rCouncil Member Lujan moved to amend Resolution 07-4643 to constitute the Parks and Recreation Commission with a total of five (5) members and (3)�alternates; seconded by Mayor Perez. The motion unanimously carried by the following roll call vote: AYES: Solis, Storing, Lujan, Chavez, and Perez. NOES: None.\r\rVoting was opened for the�appointment of one (1) member to the Parks and Recreation Commission.\r\rActing City Clerk Giron announced the votes.��Council Member Solis voted to appoint Mike Salas, Mayor Pro Tem Storing�voted to appoint Roger Clark, Council Member Chavez voted to appoint Mike Salas, Council Member Lujan voted to appoint Mike Salas, and Mayor Lou Perez voted for Jennifer Gonzalez.\r\rActing City Clerk Giron announced that Mike Salas qualified as the fifth member of the Commission.\r\rCity Attorney Casso noted that pursuant to Council action, the remaining applicants (Mr. Clark, Ms. Gonzalez, and Ms. Meza) would serve as alternates.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39593\" \u0014CITY COUNCIL CONSENT CALENDAR \u0015\u0007\u0007\rCouncil Member Chavez moved to approve Consent Calendar Items No. D-1 through D-9, with the exception of Item No. D-5; seconded by Council Member Lujan.\r\rCouncil Member Solis requested that Item No. D-5 be pulled from the Consent Calendar for separate consideration.\r\rThe motion unanimously carried by the following roll call vote: AYES: Solis, Storing, Lujan, Chavez, and Perez. NOES: None.\r\rD-1\u0007APPROVAL OF RESOLUTION APPROVING WARRANT REGISTER NO. 1210 FOR FISCAL YEAR 2007-08 \u0007\u0007\rStaff Recommendation:� It is recommended that the City Council adopt the resolution.\r\rD-2\u0007APPROVAL OF NEW PARTICIPANT(S) FOR CDBG HOUSING REHABILITATION (D97301-08) - FISCAL YEAR 2007-08 \u0007\u0007\rStaff Recommendation:� The� Screening Commission recommends that the City Council approve the allocations and authorize the Assistant City� Manager to execute the necessary documents to implement the Housing Rehabilitation Program in the amount of $17,000.\r\rD-3\u0007SECOND READING - EXTENSION OF ORDINANCE NO. 06-856 EXTENDING THE TERMS AND PROVISIONS OF URGENCY ORDINANCE NO. O6-853 - PROHIBITING ESTABLISHMENT OR OPERATION OF \"SMOKE SHOPS\" IN THE CITY OF LA PUENTE (Introduced and title read at meeting of August 28, 2007) \u0007\u0007\rStaff Recommendation:� It is recommended that the City Council Adopt the ordinance extending Ordinance No. 06-856 for and additional year.\r\rD-4\u0007AUTHORIZATION TO SOLICIT BIDS FOR PURCHASE OF A NEW 2007 CHEVROLET SILVERADO 2500 HD CLASSIC 2WD FOR THE MAINTENANCE SUPERVISOR \u0007\u0007\rStaff Recommendation:� It is recommended that the City Council authorize Staff to solicit bids for the purchase of a new 2007 Chevrolet Silverado 2500 HD Classic 2WD Regular Cab 133\" Work Truck and designate Tuesday, October 16, 2007 at 10:00 a.m. as the deadline for receiving bids.\r\rD-6\u0007BID AWARD:� LOCAL STREET RESURFACING (AMAR, PUENTE, TONOPAH) PROJECT \u0007\u0007\rStaff Recommendation:� It is recommended that the City Council award the contract for the construction portion of the Local Street Resurfacing (Amar, Puente, Tonopah) Project to Silvia Construction.\r\rD-7\u0007CONSIDERATION OF AMENDING THE 2007-2008 BUDGET TO INCLUDE THE COSTS FOR CAPITAL IMPROVEMENT PROGRAM (CIP) TO BE FUNDED UNDER THE SEWER ENTERPRISE FUND AND TO AMEND FUNDING SOURCES OF ALL STREET IMPROVEMENTS CIP PROJECTS \u0007\u0007\rStaff Recommendation:� It is recommended that the City Council adopt the resolution approving the City�s updated Capital Improvement Projects and amend the budget to include the costs for the projects in the City�s 2007/2008 Fiscal Year Budget.\r\rD-8\u0007AUTHORIZATION TO SOLICIT BIDS FOR TEMPLE AVENUE STREET IMPROVEMENT PROJECT FROM GLENDORA AVENUE TO STIMSON AVENUE \u0007\u0007\rStaff Recommendation:� It is recommended that the City Council: (1) approve the specifications; and (2) authorize Staff to solicit bids for the Temple Avenue Street Improvement Project from Glendora Avenue to Stimson Avenue.\r\rD-9\u0007AWARD OF CONTRACT FOR THE INSTALLATION OF AN AUDIO/VISUAL SYSTEM FOR THE SENIOR CENTER IMPROVEMENTS PROJECT \u0007\u0007\rStaff Recommendation:� It is recommended that the City Council award the bid to Western Audio Visual Corporation in the amount of $23,809.40 and authorize the Mayor to execute the Agreement with Western Audio Visual Corporation for installation of the Audio/Visual system at the Senior Center.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=46685\" \u0014ITEM PULLED FROM CONSENT CALENDAR FOR SEPARATE CONSIDERATION \u0015\u0007\u0007\rD-5\u0007AUTHORIZATION TO SOLICIT BIDS FOR PURCHASE OF A NEW 2007 FORD ESCAPE HYBRID FWD FOR THE PUBLIC WORKS DIRECTOR \u0007\u0007\rCouncil Member Solis moved to table this item until the performance of the newly appointed Public Works Director can be assessed; seconded by Mayor Pro Tem Storing.\r\rMayor Pro Tem Storing clarified that she seconded the motion only to discuss the item.\r\rCity Manager Cowley provided background information on this item. She noted that the Public Works Director is on call 7 days per week, 24 hours a day. This item was previously budgeted and comes from Air Quality Management funds, not the General Fund. \r\rMayor Pro Tem Storing moved to solicit bids for purchase of a new 2007 Ford Escape Hybrid FWD and designate Tuesday, October 16, 2007 at 11:00 A.M. as the deadline for receiving bids; seconded by Council Member Lujan. The motion carried by the following roll call vote: AYES: Storing, Lujan, Chavez, and Perez. NOES: Solis.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39617\" \u0014NEW BUSINESS TO BE CONSIDERED BY THE CITY COUNCIL \u0015\u0007\u0007\rE-1\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39618\" \u0014CONSIDERATION OF INTRODUCTION OF AN ORDINANCE INCREASING COUNCIL MEMBERS� SALARIES PURSUANT TO GOVERNMENT CODE SECTION 36516 \u0015\u0007\u0007\rCity Manager Cowley provided the staff report and noted the historical background of the adjustments�to City Council salaries.\r\r\r\rIn response to an inquiry from Council Member Solis, City Manager Cowley and City Attorney Casso clarified the effective dates of the new compensation if the Council were to approve this item. \r\rCouncil Member Lujan moved to (1) read the ordinance by title only and waive further reading; and (2) introduce the Ordinance for subsequent adoption; seconded by Mayor Perez. The motion failed by the following roll call vote: AYES: Lujan, and Perez.� NOES: Solis, Storing, and Chavez.\r\rE-2\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39619\" \u0014CONSIDERATION OF FORMATION OF LA PUENTE PUBLIC FINANCING AUTHORITY \u0015\u0007\u0007\rMr. Anderson, from the City's Financial Advisory Group, provided a brief staff report on the item.� The formation of a formal Public Financing Authority allows the Authority to issue bonds and govern other related administrative issues.\r\rIn response to an inquiry from Council Member Solis, Mr. Anderson noted that there was no cost to form the Authority and that his company's schedule of fees had been previously approved by the Council.\r\rIn response to an inquiry from Council Member Lujan, Mr. Anderson noted that most cities who issue bonds have a Public Financing Authority.\r\rMayor Perez moved to adopt the Resolution authorizing Execution and Delivery of a Joint Exercise of Powers Agreement with the La Puente Community Development Commission, Establishing the La Puente Public Financing Authority; seconded by Council Member Chavez. The motion unanimously carried by the following roll call vote: AYES: Solis, Storing, Lujan, Chavez, and Perez.� NOES: None.\r\rE-3\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39620\" \u0014REQUEST TO CONSTRUCT A MONUMENT IN HONOR OF ALL LOCAL VETERANS FROM EVERY BRANCH OF THE SERVICE ON THE TRIANGLE PROPERTY LOCATED AT THE ENTRANCE OF CENTRAL AVENUE AND ABBEY STREET (Requested by Council Member Solis) \u0015\u0007\u0007\rCouncil Member Solis moved to direct staff to research costs related to the construction of a Veteran�s Memorial; seconded by Mayor Pro Tem Storing.\r\rIn response to an inquiry from Mayor Pro Tem Storing, Council Member Solis clarified the type of Veteran�s Memorial that he would like to see the City construct.� Council Member Storing affirmed her support for such a project.\r\rCouncil Member Lujan expressed his support for veterans and clarified his concerns regarding the dedication of staff time�on researching unbudgeted and unfunded capital improvement projects for this fiscal year.\r\rCouncil Member Solis�noted his commitment to a project that would create an area of reflection and solace for the Veterans.\r\rCouncil Member Chavez noted that she would be in support of staff taking the time to research costs incurred by other cities in constructing their Veteran�s Memorials. \r\rThe motion carried by the following roll call vote: AYES: Solis, Storing, Chavez, and Perez. NOES: Lujan.\r\rCity Manager Cowley said the results of the research would be presented at the mid-year budget study session.\r\rIn response to an inquiry from Mayor Pro Tem Storing, Assistant City Manager Yamachika briefly clarified the funding sources for the Nature Education Center project. \r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=47806\" \u0014RECESS CITY COUNCIL AND CONVENE THE COMMUNITY DEVELOPMENT COMMISSION \u0015\u0007\u0007\rThe City Council recessed and convened the Special Meeting of the Community Development Commission at 7:54 p.m.\r\rAt 8:02 p.m. the City Council reconvened.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39680\" \u0014COUNCIL AB1234 REPORTS \u0015\u0007\u0007\rMayor Perez made an AB 1234 report related to his attendance at the League of California Cities Conference in Sacramento.� He also met with Assemblyman Ed Hernandez and Lieutenant Governor John Garamendi while attending the conference.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39683\" \u0014ORAL COMMENTS FROM COUNCIL\u0015 \u0007\u0007\rCouncil Member�Lujan reported that the National League of Cities is accepting applications from elected officials for volunteer positions currently available on various committees.\r\rCouncil Member�Solis noted the recent accomplishments of the La Puente Girl�s Softball League.\r\rMayor�Perez noted that the City Council�would adjourn in memory of Anthony Gonzales, who died on September 6, 2007 as a result of a traffic accident.\r\rMayor Pro Tem�Storing�congratulated staff for the Concerts in the Park series.\r\rCouncil Member�Solis congratulated staff for the Movies in the Park Program.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39686\" \u0014ORAL COMMENTS FROM STAFF\u0015 \u0007\u0007\rNone. \r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=46708\" \u0014RECONVENE SPECIAL CITY COUNCIL MEETING \u0015\u0007\u0007\rThe Mayor convened the Special City Council meeting at 8:07 p.m.\r\r\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39689\" \u0014RECESS TO CLOSED SESSION \u0015\u0007\u0007\rAt 8:08 p.m. City Attorney Casso announced that the City Council would recess to Closed Session pursuant Government Code Section 54957.6.\r\rF-3\u0007\u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://lapuente.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=&clip_id=248&meta_id=39692\" \u0014THE CITY COUNCIL WILL RECESS TO CLOSED SESSION PURSUANT TO GOVERNMENT CODE SECTION 54957.6 \u0015\u0007\u0007\rAGENCY NEGOTIATOR: Carol Cowley, City Manager\r\rEMPLOYEE ORGANIZATION: SEIU Local 721\r\r\u0007RECONVENE TO OPEN SESSION \u0007\u0007\rAt 9:03�p.m. the City Council reconvened to open session at which time the City Attorney announced City Council had recessed to closed session.� Council�gave direction to the City Manager on a 5-0 vote�to negotiate with�SEIU Local 721. \r�\r\u0007ADJOURNMENT \u0007\u0007\rThere being no further business to come before the City Council, Mayor Perez adjourned the meeting in memory Anthony Gonzalez at 9:03�p.m.\r\r\r\r______________________________ \rDiana Giron, Acting City Clerk \u0007______________________________ \rLouis R. Perez, Mayor \u0007\u0007\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\rLA PUENTE CITY COUNCIL SEPTEMBER 11, 2007\rMINUTES PAGE \u0013 PAGE \u00147\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0007\b\u0000\u0000 \b\u0000\u0000\u0012\b\u0000\u0000\u0013\b\u0000\u0000\u001f\b\u0000\u0000\"\b\u0000\u00004\b\u0000\u00006\b\u0000\u0000H\b\u0000\u0000I\b\